.TH SHMDT 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
shmdt \- detach a System V shared memory segment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/shm.h>
.B int shmdt(const void* address);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Detaches the segment at the original address returned by shmat. A segment
marked for removal is destroyed after its last attachment is detached.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero, or \-1 with errno set. Success leaves errno unchanged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shmat (3crunch),
.BR shmctl (3crunch),
.BR shmdt (2)
